# Copy to .env (gitignored — this value is specific to this machine/session,
# not secret, see CLAUDE.md § Pièges "Backend depuis l'iPhone").
#
# The URL of the allow-list gateway (tools/api-gateway/), reached through an
# ngrok tunnel — not the Next.js server directly. MUST include the
# /api/mobile/v1 prefix: `src/services/api.ts` appends paths like
# `/auth/login` directly to this value, and the gateway only forwards paths
# starting with /api/mobile/v1/ — anything else (including a request missing
# that prefix) gets a 404 from the gateway itself, never reaching Next.js.
# Get the domain from your ngrok dashboard (Gateway → Domains), start the
# gateway with `npm run gateway`, then `ngrok http 3200 --url https://<your-domain>`.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ values are inlined in plain text in the built app — fine here,
# this is a public tunnel URL, never a secret.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://your-subdomain.ngrok-free.dev/api/mobile/v1"
